            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Looking forward to when this goes in \ud83d\udcaf\n\nOverall it would be really useful for me \ud83d\udc4d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 49,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "can you use `sdbusplus::object_path` for any variables that represent actual object paths? i feel like its going to be easier to tell things apart that way and it gives helper functions"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 49,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yash Patel",
                        "email": "yash.pateltx@gmail.com",
                        "username": "pebbleeee"
                    },
                    "message": "Done, AssocRow fields and the assocEndpoints map now use sdbusplus::object_path throughout, and filename()/parent_path() replace the manual rfind/substr logic."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 49,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you \ud83d\udc4d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 53,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: i am wondering if it would be ok to do the same trick as the bmcweb cli and just roll this tool into the main mapper binary then use a symlink or wrapper script or commandline option to select between daemon and cli.\n\ne.g.\n`mapper --service`\nand \n`mapper assocs -t probing`\n\nmaybe it would save a few bytes in the overall fw binary.\n\nFeel free to discard this comment if you prefer the traditional standalone binary."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 73,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "In the future I can see adding additional options, so I think it would be good to keep the main() function small and make this lambda be a proper function."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 73,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yash Patel",
                        "email": "yash.pateltx@gmail.com",
                        "username": "pebbleeee"
                    },
                    "message": "Done, extracted to dumpAssocs(), main() is now just CLI setup with a one-liner callback."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 73,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 126,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "`sdbusplus::object_path` has helper functions like `.filename()` and `.parent_path()` that do all of this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 126,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yash Patel",
                        "email": "yash.pateltx@gmail.com",
                        "username": "pebbleeee"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 190,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: \n\nI'm not a big fan of aligning this since the output will already be large due to path length.\n\nMaybe better to just structure it as 2 lines per association?\n\nFeel free to ignore this comment if you disagree, it is just minor detail which can be changed later and kind of subjective."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 190,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "We'd be open to ideas still, even if adding other options to control the formatting.\n\nA 2 line version could maybe be like:\n\n```\n/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/chassis/motherboard/fan0 | sensors\n/xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/fan_tach/fan0_0                   | inventory\n\n/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/chassis/motherboard/fan1 | sensors\n/xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/fan_tach/fan1_0                   | inventory\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 190,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "if it is only for humans to look at we could also extract the longest common prefix\nto make the output more compact\n\n```\nprefix /xyz/openbmc_project/\n\ninventory/system/chassis/motherboard/fan0\n    sensors -> <- inventory sensors/fan_tach/fan0_0\n\ninventory/system/chassis/motherboard/fan1\n    sensors -> <- inventory sensors/fan_tach/fan1_0\n```"
                }
            ],
