            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 98,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I saw a situation today where we might have:\nchassis/contains <-> fan/contained_by\nand\nchassis/cooled_by <-> fan/cooling\n\nWould that break this?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 104,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "`parent_path()` never returns an empty string, so we can drop this check?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/mappertool.cpp",
                    "line": 128,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "my query: why are you checking `reverseAssocPath` for empty string?\n\nWith correct usage `sdbusplus::object_path` can be no shorter than `\"/\"`.\n\nSee https://dbus.freedesktop.org/doc/dbus-specification.html#basic-types\n\nquote:\n\n```\n\n          The following rules define a valid object path. Implementations must\n          not send or accept messages with invalid object paths.\n          \n\n                The path may be of any length.\n              \n                The path must begin with an ASCII '/' (integer 47) character,\n                and must consist of elements separated by slash characters.\n              \n                Each element must only contain the ASCII characters\n                \"[A-Z][a-z][0-9]_\"\n              \n                No element may be the empty string.\n              \n                Multiple '/' characters cannot occur in sequence.\n              \n                A trailing '/' character is not allowed unless the\n                path is the root path (a single '/' character).\n              \n```"
                }
            ],
